WEBVTT

00:00:00.406 --> 00:00:04.985
In this video, you will use your location on the map, and learn what happens to it.

00:00:04.985 --> 00:00:06.207
We start at the website.

00:00:07.057 --> 00:00:11.401
To begin, open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:11.401 --> 00:00:13.262
That is the only address you need.

00:00:16.092 --> 00:00:18.512
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:18.512 --> 00:00:21.814
The first time you visit, it asks to use your location.

00:00:21.814 --> 00:00:23.370
Tap Use my location.

00:00:25.053 --> 00:00:29.071
That is how the map shows how far things are, and gives you directions.

00:00:29.071 --> 00:00:32.154
Your browser asks permission as well, so tap Allow.

00:00:34.042 --> 00:00:39.442
Your location is used only on your device, and you can say no at any time.

00:00:39.442 --> 00:00:41.535
The map zooms to where you are.

00:00:41.535 --> 00:00:45.461
There are no events on your street, so tap Show all of Southern California.

00:00:47.117 --> 00:00:51.909
Now every place shows how far away it is, nearest first, so you can plan your drive.

00:00:52.777 --> 00:00:57.483
Any time you want to come back to where you are, tap the location button on the map.

00:00:57.483 --> 00:01:00.142
It is the small circle with a target.

00:01:00.142 --> 00:01:06.069
Your location is used on your device, to center the map and to estimate drive times.

00:01:06.069 --> 00:01:08.714
It is not sent to our servers for that.

00:01:08.714 --> 00:01:10.430
There is one exception.

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:18.082
On a home, the button I saw it lit tonight sends your position to our server once, only to check that you are within about a quarter mile.

00:01:18.082 --> 00:01:19.406
We do not store it.

00:01:19.406 --> 00:01:21.152
We keep only a yes or no.

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:26.466
You can always decline to share your location.

00:01:26.466 --> 00:01:27.972
Everything still works.

00:01:27.972 --> 00:01:30.368
You just will not see distances.

00:01:30.368 --> 00:01:33.423
That is how location works on SoCal Lights.

00:01:33.423 --> 00:01:36.737
It stays on your device, unless you tap I saw it lit tonight.

00:01:38.109 --> 00:01:40.049
Next up: Pricing in two minutes.
